{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Has the favor ceased?</b> — [This is] a noun, and the plural is חנינות, and the meaning is from the derivation of חנון. And חנון is a פָּעוֹל form for the word שכח. Likewise רחמיו for the word קפץ."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "The lemma and the Hebrew words שכח and קפץ are here understood as roots meaning 'to cease/end'; Ibn Ezra argues that חנון and רחמים are nominal forms built from roots meaning 'to cease,' i.e., divine favor that has ceased."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:47.564318760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}